Day 74 /100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge
Solved LeetCode 1373 – Maximum Sum BST in Binary Tree today!
- Approach:
I used post-order traversal to process the left and right subtrees before the current node.
For every subtree, I keep track of:
min → minimum value 
max → maximum value 
sum → sum of all nodes 
A subtree is a valid BST when:
 left.max < root.val < right.min
If it is a BST, I calculate its sum and update the maximum answer.

Time: O(n)
Space: O(h) 

- Takeaways:
 Post-order traversal is very useful when the parent depends on information from its children. 
 Returning multiple properties from recursion makes complex tree problems much easier.

